[38;5;252m[1m## What the library is[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mc_src/[0m is a small macro-driven arithmetic driver. [38;5;10mmdmacros.h[0m is pure preprocessor machinery that token-pastes an operation family ([38;5;10mOP[0m ∈ [38;5;10madd|sub|mul[0m) and manually unrolls [38;5;10mREPEAT[0m ∈ [38;5;10m0..7[0m accumulator steps. [38;5;10mmdcore.c[0m exports 6 functions + 2 globals; [38;5;10mmdmain.c[0m composes them. Note [38;5;10mCMakeLists.txt[0m only builds an [3mexecutable[23m, so I compiled the [38;5;10m.so[0m myself with [38;5;10mgcc -shared -fPIC[0m (nothing in [38;5;10mc_src/[0m was modified — all output goes to [38;5;10mcbuild/[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## The bug that was found[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mmdcore.c[0m declares [38;5;10mint (*G_OP)(int,int)[0m and [38;5;10mconst char *G_OP_NAME[0m — neither pointer [3mobject[23m is [38;5;10mconst[0m, so gcc puts both in writable [38;5;10m.data[0m, and an external caller can legitimately [38;5;10mdlsym("G_OP")[0m and overwrite it (I confirmed this works against the C [38;5;10m.so[0m). The translation used immutable Rust [38;5;10mstatic[0ms, which LLVM marks [38;5;10mconstant[0m and the linker places in [38;5;10m.data.rel.ro[0m — mapped [1mread-only[22m by RELRO. The same store that succeeds against C segfaulted against Rust. Changed both to [38;5;10mstatic mut[0m so they land in [38;5;10m.data[0m; [38;5;10mreadelf[0m now shows identical placement.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Everything else in the translation was already faithful, including the two things most likely to be "fixed" by mistake: [38;5;10mDISPATCH_REP[0m has no [38;5;10mcase 7[0m, so [38;5;10muse_generated(7)[0m silently returns [38;5;10mINIT_<OP>[0m rather than accumulating — and with [38;5;10mREPEAT=7[0m that is exactly what [38;5;10mmain[0m calls. The Rust reproduces this.[0m[0m
